          "httpVersion": "HTTP/1.1",
          "method": "GET",
          "queryString": [],
          "url": "http://localhost:8002/v1/repositories/05511578-6e37-5843-96b9-d9e017fd6ca6/commits/f12cffb97ee8e0416f18570ff57f02e13beb6dbf"
        },
        "response": {
          "bodySize": 6020,
          "content": {
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "size": 6020,
            "text": "{\"sha\":\"f12cffb97ee8e0416f18570ff57f02e13beb6dbf\",\"parents\":[\"c77869250658d76a185813ac186914c14dccbc7e\"],\"message\":\"fix: drop environment/Dockerfile for docker_image so the task runs on a plane, and move the agent to Sonnet 5.5 (#17)\\n\\nProblem: the Introspection Harbor adapter refuses a task whose\\nenvironment/Dockerfile nothing on a plane builds (unused_dockerfile),\\nbecause the Runtime image fills main there; deleting the file alone\\nleaves Harbor's local Docker provider composing main from it.\\n\\nObjective: main's task must run as a kind: eval trial on a plane, and\\nthe local Docker trial must still get an agent container, now from\\ntask.toml's docker_image (buildpack-deps:noble-curl: Ubuntu 24.04 with\\nca-certificates and curl, what the Dockerfile built). The agent moves\\nfrom claude-sonnet-4-6 to claude-sonnet-5-5.\\n\\n\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XR2prAhtGPTsPw6GEqGRFZ\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Christoforus Yoga Haryanto\",\"email\":\"cyharyanto@gmail.com\",\"date\":\"2026-11-02T14:13:09+11:00\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"GitHub\",\"email\":null,\"date\":\"2026-11-02T14:13:09+11:00\"},\"files\":[{\"filename\":\"README.md\",\"status\":\"modified\",\"additions\":4,\"deletions\":3,\"changes\":7},{\"filename\":\"agents/agent.yaml\",\"status\":\"modified\",\"additions\":1,\"deletions\":1,\"changes\":2},{\"filename\":\"harbor/environment/Dockerfile\",\"status\":\"removed\",\"additions\":0,\"deletions\":8,\"changes\":8},{\"filename\":\"harbor/environment/docker-compose.yaml\",\"status\":\"modified\",\"additions\":1,\"deletions\":1,\"changes\":2},{\"filename\":\"harbor/task.toml\",\"status\":\"modified\",\"additions\":4,\"deletions\":0,\"changes\":4},{\"filename\":\"scripts/run-local.sh\",\"status\":\"modified\",\"additions\":1,\"deletions\":1,\"changes\":2}],\"patch\":\"diff --git a/README.md b/README.md\\nindex 8043910..a53d836 100644\\n--- a/README.md\\n+++ b/README.md\\n@@ -20,9 +20,8 @@ it resolves to.\\n ```text\\n harbor/                                the Harbor task, laid out as harbor/examples/tasks/<name>\\n ├── instruction.md                     the prompt\\n-├── task.toml                          Harbor task metadata + [[environment.mcp_servers]]\\n+├── task.toml                          Harbor task metadata, `docker_image` + [[environment.mcp_servers]]\\n ├── environment/\\n-│   ├── Dockerfile                     the agent container for a local Docker trial\\n │   ├── docker-compose.yaml            the world: `main` (the agent slot) + `mcp-server`\\n │   └── mcp-server/\\n │       ├── Dockerfile                 the mcp-server image\\n@@ -37,9 +36,11 @@ agents/agent.yaml                      the Recipe agent; uses `hello-mcp` `echo`\\n ```\\n \\n `docker-compose.yaml` is Harbor's shape and stays verbatim. The service named\\n-`main` is the agent: Harbor configures it from `environment/Dockerfile` for a\\n+`main` is the agent: Harbor runs it from `task.toml`'s `docker_image` for a\\n local trial, and the Introspection Runtime image fills the same slot for a\\n platform trial, so `main` carries only `depends_on` and (if needed) `volumes`.\\n+The task carries no `environment/Dockerfile`: nothing on the platform would\\n+build it, so the Introspection Harbor adapter refuses a task that has one.\\n Every other service is the world. On the platform each becomes a container of\\n the sandbox pod, started before the agent in `depends_on` order, reached by its\\n compose name on the pod's loopback, under the same gVisor sandbox and network\\ndiff --git a/agents/agent.yaml b/agents/agent.yaml\\nindex a7d89e9..7a414e3 100644\\n--- a/agents/agent.yaml\\n+++ b/agents/agent.yaml\\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\\n name: agent\\n description: Calls the hello MCP for the Harbor task\\n ai:\\n-  model: anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6\\n+  model: anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5\\n   thinking_level: low\\n tools:\\n   - read\\ndiff --git a/harbor/environment/Dockerfile b/harbor/environment/Dockerfile\\ndeleted file mode 100644\\nindex b4d2951..0000000\\n--- a/harbor/environment/Dockerfile\\n+++ /dev/null\\n@@ -1,8 +0,0 @@\\n-FROM ubuntu:24.04\\n-\\n-RUN apt-get update && DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive apt-get install -y \\\\\\n-    ca-certificates \\\\\\n-    curl \\\\\\n-    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*\\n-\\n-WORKDIR /app\\ndiff --git a/harbor/environment/docker-compose.yaml b/harbor/environment/docker-compose.yaml\\nindex aa3e3ec..c088c3e 100644\\n--- a/harbor/environment/docker-compose.yaml\\n+++ b/harbor/environment/docker-compose.yaml\\n@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@\\n # The task's world, in Harbor's shape. `main` is the agent container: Harbor\\n-# configures it from environment/Dockerfile for a local Docker trial, and the\\n+# runs it from task.toml's docker_image for a local Docker trial, and the\\n # Introspection Runtime image fills the same slot when the trial runs as an\\n # eval task, so `main` carries only what binds the agent to the world.\\n #\\ndiff --git a/harbor/task.toml b/harbor/task.toml\\nindex 7d799aa..dbcab7c 100644\\n--- a/harbor/task.toml\\n+++ b/harbor/task.toml\\n@@ -13,6 +13,10 @@ timeout_sec = 60.0\\n timeout_sec = 600.0\\n \\n [environment]\\n+# The agent container for a local Docker trial. An image, not a Dockerfile: on\\n+# the platform the Runtime image fills `main`, and the Introspection Harbor\\n+# adapter refuses an environment/Dockerfile that nothing there builds.\\n+docker_image = \\\"buildpack-deps:noble-curl\\\"\\n build_timeout_sec = 600.0\\n cpus = 1\\n memory_mb = 2048\\ndiff --git a/scripts/run-local.sh b/scripts/run-local.sh\\nindex 238910e..d01a0ba 100755\\n--- a/scripts/run-local.sh\\n+++ b/scripts/run-local.sh\\n@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@\\n # plane involved at all.\\n #\\n # This is the shape that verifies the task itself: `docker compose` brings up\\n-# `main` from environment/Dockerfile and `mcp-server` from its build context,\\n+# `main` from task.toml's docker_image and `mcp-server` from its build context,\\n # on a compose network, and Harbor's verifier reads the result. Nothing here\\n # uploads an image, creates a task, or needs a credential beyond the model key\\n # the agent uses — so a failure here is the task's, not the platform's.\\n\"}"
          },
